  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "Chef gave you a sequence of integers a1,a2,…,aNa_1, a_2, \\dots, a_Na1​,a2​,…,aN​ and 333 integers KKK, mmm and xxx. Let's define the following functions:\nG(i1,…,iK)=gcd(ai1,…,aiK)G(i_1, \\ldots, i_K) = \\mathrm{gcd}\\left(a_{i_1}, \\dots, a_{i_K}\\right)G(i1​,…,iK​)=gcd(ai1​​,…,aiK​​)\nSx(i1,…,iK)=ai1x+ai2x+…+aiKxS_x(i_1, \\ldots, i_K) = a_{i_1}^x + a_{i_2}^x + \\ldots + a_{i_K}^xSx​(i1​,…,iK​)=ai1​x​+ai2​x​+…+aiK​x​\nPm(i1,…,iK)=(ai1⋅ai2⋅…⋅aiK)mP_m(i_1, \\ldots, i_K) = \\left(a_{i_1} \\cdot a_{i_2} \\cdot \\ldots \\cdot a_{i_K}\\right)^mPm​(i1​,…,iK​)=(ai1​​⋅ai2​​⋅…⋅aiK​​)m\nW(T)=smallest  prime  divisor  of  P1(T)W(T) = \\mathrm{smallest\\,\\, prime\\,\\, divisor\\,\\, of\\,\\, } P_1(T)W(T)=smallestprimedivisorofP1​(T)\n\nChef wants you to compute the sum of G(T)⋅W(T)⋅Sx(T)⋅Pm(T)G(T) \\cdot W(T) \\cdot S_x(T) \\cdot P_m(T)G(T)⋅W(T)⋅Sx​(T)⋅Pm​(T) over all KKK-tuples of indices T=(i1,i2,…,iK)T = (i_1, i_2, \\ldots, i_K)T=(i1​,i2​,…,iK​) such that ij∈{1,2,…,N}i_j \\in \\{1, 2, \\ldots, N\\}ij​∈{1,2,…,N} for each valid jjj (there are NKN^KNK of these KKK-tuples). Since this sum could be enormous, compute it modulo 109+710^9 + 7109+7.",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤N≤1061 \\le N \\le 10^61≤N≤106",
      "1≤K,m,x≤10181 \\le K, m, x \\le 10^{18}1≤K,m,x≤1018",
      "2≤ai≤1062 \\le a_i \\le 10^62≤ai​≤106 for each valid iii",
      "Subtasks**Subtask #1 (5 points):**",
      "N≤10N \\le 10N≤10",
      "K≤6K \\le 6K≤6",
      "**Subtask #2 (20 points):** for each valid iii, aia_iai​ is even"
    ],
    "inputFormat": "The first line of the input contains four space-separated integers NNN, KKK, mmm and xxx.\nThe second line contains NNN space-separated integers a1,a2,…,aNa_1, a_2, \\ldots, a_Na1​,a2​,…,aN​.",
    "outputFormat": "Print a single line containing one integer ∑TG(T)⋅W(T)⋅Sx(T)⋅Pm(T)\\sum_T G(T) \\cdot W(T) \\cdot S_x(T) \\cdot P_m(T)∑T​G(T)⋅W(T)⋅Sx​(T)⋅Pm​(T) modulo 109+710^9+7109+7.",
    "notes": [],
