        "output": "2414",
        "explanation": "Explanation:\nExample case 1: We have NK=32=9N^K = 3^2 = 9NK=32=9 possible pairs TTT of indices. The corresponding summands are:\n\nT=(1,1)T = (1, 1)T=(1,1): gcd(2,2)⋅(21+21)⋅(2⋅2)1⋅2=64\\mathrm{gcd}(2, 2) \\cdot (2^1 + 2^1) \\cdot (2 \\cdot 2)^1 \\cdot 2 = 64gcd(2,2)⋅(21+21)⋅(2⋅2)1⋅2=64\nT=(1,2)T = (1, 2)T=(1,2): gcd(2,3)⋅(21+31)⋅(2⋅3)1⋅2=60\\mathrm{gcd}(2, 3) \\cdot (2^1 + 3^1) \\cdot (2 \\cdot 3)^1 \\cdot 2 = 60gcd(2,3)⋅(21+31)⋅(2⋅3)1⋅2=60\nT=(1,3)T = (1, 3)T=(1,3): gcd(2,4)⋅(21+41)⋅(2⋅4)1⋅2=192\\mathrm{gcd}(2, 4) \\cdot (2^1 + 4^1) \\cdot (2 \\cdot 4)^1 \\cdot 2 = 192gcd(2,4)⋅(21+41)⋅(2⋅4)1⋅2=192\nT=(2,1)T = (2, 1)T=(2,1): gcd(3,2)⋅(31+21)⋅(3⋅2)1⋅2=60\\mathrm{gcd}(3, 2) \\cdot (3^1 + 2^1) \\cdot (3 \\cdot 2)^1 \\cdot 2 = 60gcd(3,2)⋅(31+21)⋅(3⋅2)1⋅2=60\nT=(2,2)T = (2, 2)T=(2,2): gcd(3,3)⋅(31+31)⋅(3⋅3)1⋅3=486\\mathrm{gcd}(3, 3) \\cdot (3^1 + 3^1) \\cdot (3 \\cdot 3)^1 \\cdot 3 = 486gcd(3,3)⋅(31+31)⋅(3⋅3)1⋅3=486\nT=(2,3)T = (2, 3)T=(2,3): gcd(3,4)⋅(31+41)⋅(3⋅4)1⋅2=168\\mathrm{gcd}(3, 4) \\cdot (3^1 + 4^1) \\cdot (3 \\cdot 4)^1 \\cdot 2 = 168gcd(3,4)⋅(31+41)⋅(3⋅4)1⋅2=168\nT=(3,1)T = (3, 1)T=(3,1): gcd(4,2)⋅(41+21)⋅(4⋅2)1⋅2=192\\mathrm{gcd}(4, 2) \\cdot (4^1 + 2^1) \\cdot (4 \\cdot 2)^1 \\cdot 2 = 192gcd(4,2)⋅(41+21)⋅(4⋅2)1⋅2=192\nT=(3,2)T = (3, 2)T=(3,2): gcd(4,3)⋅(41+31)⋅(4⋅3)1⋅2=168\\mathrm{gcd}(4, 3) \\cdot (4^1 + 3^1) \\cdot (4 \\cdot 3)^1 \\cdot 2 = 168gcd(4,3)⋅(41+31)⋅(4⋅3)1⋅2=168\nT=(3,3)T = (3, 3)T=(3,3): gcd(4,4)⋅(41+41)⋅(4⋅4)1⋅2=1024\\mathrm{gcd}(4, 4) \\cdot (4^1 + 4^1) \\cdot (4 \\cdot 4)^1 \\cdot 2 = 1024gcd(4,4)⋅(41+41)⋅(4⋅4)1⋅2=1024\n\nTheir sum modulo 109+710^9+7109+7 is 241424142414."
